column2:
Victory, Krishna, lord of the world; victory, destroyer of all sins; victory, slayer of Chanura and Keshin; victory, destroyer of Kamsa;
brahmapuran:57:34	victory, lotus-eyed one; victory, bearer of discus and mace; victory, dark as a blue cloud; victory, giver of all happiness;
brahmapuran:57:35	victory, god worshipped by the world; victory, destroyer of worldly existence; victory, lord of the worlds, master; victory, giver of the fruit of wishes.
brahmapuran:57:36	In the terrible ocean of worldly existence, without substance, foaming with sorrow, full of the crocodiles of anger, fierce, flooded with the waters of sense-objects,
brahmapuran:57:37	muddy with the waves of various diseases, very hard to cross with whirlpools of delusion — I am sunk, O best of gods; save me, Purushottama.
